  "title": "Community models grew beyond text",
  "summary": "The catalog grew in several directions this week, while community publishing and the APIs around those models became easier to use.\n\nCommunity providers can register OpenAI-compatible image endpoints, putting text-to-image models alongside community text models in the catalog. Publishers gained a request path for public access, owners gained deactivate and reactivate controls, and creators can now set readable display titles without changing callable slugs. App submissions also moved to an issue form that no longer requires Enter registration.\n\nGemini 3.6 Flash, Gemini Flash Lite 3.5, LongCat 2.0, Laguna S 2.1, and Claude Opus 5 joined or refreshed their catalog entries. LongCat and Laguna each offer a 1,048,576-token context window; `claude-large` now points to Opus 5 and remains paid-only. CSM 1B added speech generation with six voices and five output formats.\n\n`cohere-embed-v4` added text-and-image inputs and retrieval roles, while `qwen3-embedding-8b` gained a 40,960-token context limit. `gemini-2` moved to Gemini Embedding 2's GA endpoint. Its vectors are in a different space, so stored preview-era vectors need re-embedding before comparison. Model descriptions and search also became easier to navigate.\n\nLyria 3 Clip added prompt-to-music generation as a fixed 30-second MP3. Recraft V4.1 Vector added SVG generation and reference-image editing, with image responses preserving SVG output. Basic Grok Imagine image generation and editing now request 2K, while community image endpoints offer another route from prompts to pixels.",
